        '8. Alcohol Glycosides',
        'Alcohol Glycosides are a class of glycosides defined by their chemical structure, specifically by containing',
        'an alcohol as their aglycone (the non-sugar component).',
        'Salicin, Populin (benzoyl salicin), and Glucovanillic alcohol contain alcohol glycosides.',
        '1. Salicin',
        'Origin/Source: Salicin is an alcohol glycoside obtained from the stem bark of several species of',
        'Populus (poplar) trees. The principal sources include Salix purpurea and Salix fragilis.',
        'Hydrolysis: Upon hydrolysis, salicin yields glucose and salicyl alcohol (saligenin).',
        'Uses and Properties: Salicin possesses ant rheumatic properties. Its action is very closely related',
        'to salicylic acid, and it is likely oxidized to salicylic acid within the human system.',
        '2. Populin (benzoyl salicin)',
        'Hydrolysis: Upon hydrolysis, populin yields one molecule of salicyl alcohol, one molecule of benzoic',
