        "Acid-fast organisms are red, other organisms are blue **Mycobacterium smegmatis ** **Mycobacterium leprae **",
        "### Special Straining:",
        "Negative staining",
        "Capsule",
        "Endospore",
        "Flagellum",
        "Pili",
        "In negative staining technique the background is stained, and bacteria remains colorless. When this preparation is examined microscopically with low intensity of light a phase like effect is observed. Capsules appear as halo or light ring around each cell against dark background. Nigrosine stain is used for negative stain. E.g. Negative stain of cocci.",
        "Negative Staining:",
        "** Transparent Capsule around Cells ** ** Streptococci **",
        "Capsule Staining (MUIR'S METHOD) o Make smear o Apply crystal violet o Rinse with copper sulphate ** Streptococcus lactis ** ** Klebsiella pneumoniae**",
        "Spore Staining:",
        "Make smear",
        "Apply Malachite green",
